    "mu7fpvmx114wfqvaw": {
      "title": "/expressionsheet — la misma cara en varias emociones",
      "customPrompt": "/expressionsheet If the user attaches an image, you must apply only the style to it, ensuring the original image remains completely unchanged; in other words, you must recreate the user-provided image and apply solely the requested style. all visible text and labels must be written in Spanish with no English words.\nThe generated image must have four rows, and each row will contain three images.\n\n1. **Pain**  \n   *Features:* Heavily furrowed brow, eyes squeezed shut or squinting, wrinkled nose, and mouth tense or open, revealing teeth.\n2. **Laughter (genuine joy)**  \n   *Features:* Corners of the mouth turned up, raised cheeks, and wrinkles at the outer corners of the eyes (*crow's feet* / Duchenne smile).\n3. **Boisterous laughter**  \n   *Features:* Mouth wide open, eyes nearly closed due to cheek contraction, head tilted slightly back, and possible presence of tears.\n4. **Anger / Fury**  \n   *Features:* Eyebrows lowered, straight, and drawn close together; intense, fixed stare; flared nostrils; and firmly clenched jaw or lips.\n5. **Surprise**  \n   *Features:* Arched, raised eyebrows; wide-open eyes revealing the sclera (whites of the eyes); and dropped jaw forming an \"O\" shape with the mouth.\n6. **Disgust / Repugnance**  \n   *Features:* Wrinkled bridge of the nose, raised upper lip (often revealing upper teeth), and slightly narrowed eyes.\n7. **Sadness / Desolation**  \n   *Features:* Inner corners of the eyebrows raised toward the center of the forehead, downturned corners of the mouth, and a gaze that is unfocused or directed downward.\n8. **Relief**  \n   *Features:* Sudden release of tension in facial muscles, eyes gently closing or narrowing, visible exhalation, and a slight, calm smile. 9.  **Playfulness / Flirtatiousness**  \n    *Traits:* Head slightly tilted or angled downward with the gaze directed upward through the eyelashes, and a subtle half-smile.\n10. Pensive (Contemplation / Reflection)\nThe expression of someone processing internal information or recalling something. There is no aggressive tension, but rather **calm concentration and detachment from the immediate surroundings**.\n\n* **Eyes and gaze:** A \"lost\" or unfocused gaze, typically directed toward an upper corner (recalling/imagining) or toward the ground. Blinking becomes slower or less frequent.\n* **Eyebrows and forehead:** A gentle, slight furrowing of the brow (non-hostile) or one eyebrow raised slightly higher than the other, indicating active processing of doubts.\n* **Mouth:** Lips closed in a straight, relaxed line; sometimes gently pressed together or with the lower lip tucked slightly inward.\n* **Typical accompanying gesture:** Head tilted to one side, hand or knuckles resting on the chin, or the index finger lightly touching the temple or lip.\n11. Very, very sad / Desolate (Devastation / Emotional anguish)\nThis goes beyond ordinary sadness; it reflects a **total loss of hope or unbearable emotional pain**. The facial muscles struggle between giving way to a breakdown and holding back tears.\n* **Forehead and eyebrows:** The so-called *omega melancholicum* is intensely activated: the inner corners of the eyebrows rise and draw together toward the center of the forehead, creating vertical wrinkles and an inverted horseshoe-shaped curve.\n* **Eyes:** Completely brimming with tears or reddened. Eyelids appear both drooping and tense. A dull, vacant gaze—unable to focus on anything external—conveying emptiness and extreme exhaustion.\n* **Mouth and chin:** Corners of the mouth pulled sharply downward. The lower lip often trembles involuntarily. The chin wrinkles and dimples (taking on a \"cobblestone\" appearance) due to the contraction of the mentalis muscle as it tries to suppress a sob.\n* **Typical accompanying gesture:** The face seems to \"melt\" toward the ground under the pull of gravity. Head bowed, mouth slightly open exhaling shakily, or hands covering the face to hide the emotional collapse.\n* **Apathy (Total indifference)**\nThis is an active absence of interest or reaction; the face communicates a resounding **\"I couldn't care less.\"** It is characterized by a lack of energy and muscle tone.\n* **Eyes and gaze:** Heavy upper eyelids, drooping at half-mast (eyes narrowed from listlessness). The gaze drifts past without focusing on the person being spoken to, or performs a slow, lazy eye-roll. * **Forehead and eyebrows:** Completely flat, neutral, and devoid of any wrinkles or emotion. A total absence of tension.\n* **Mouth:** Lips slack, sometimes slightly parted or with a corner drooping ever so slightly in a sigh. There may be a visible puff of air that deflates the cheeks.\n* **Typical accompanying gesture:** Head tilted to the side or lolled back listlessly; jaw slack or heavily resting in the palm of the hand, accompanied by a lazy shrug."
    },
